     1|/**
     2| * IVX Unified Executive Memory (owner-only) — BLOCK 39.
     3| *
     4| * ONE durable memory API used by every higher brain — Owner AI, CRM AI,
     5| * Autonomous Mode, and the Executive Layer — so the platform stops forgetting
     6| * what it learned between sessions. It stores and retrieves the ten executive
     7| * record families the owner asked for:
     8| *   goals · projects · investors · crm_entities · owner_preferences · decisions ·
     9| *   execution_history · technical_debt · architecture_decisions · outcomes
    10| *
    11| * HARD HONESTY RULES (platform-wide, enforced here):
    12| *   - Memory NEVER fabricates content. `kind` + a non-empty `title` are required;
    13| *     unknown fields stay empty/null. `source` attributes who wrote the memory
    14| *     (owner_ai | crm_ai | autonomous_mode | executive_layer | owner | system).
    15| *   - Records are durable across process restarts (on-disk JSONL + materialised
    16| *     JSON), so a fresh process re-hydrates the full memory.
    17| *   - De-dupe by (kind + normalized title): a repeated write REFINES the existing
    18| *     memory (merges data, bumps updatedAt) instead of creating a duplicate.
    19| *
    20| * Durable layout (mirrors the proven execution-trace / investor-crm stores):
    21| *   logs/audit/unified-memory/memory.jsonl   append-only event log (source of truth)
    22| *   logs/audit/unified-memory/memory.json    materialised current state (fast reads)
    23| *
    24| * DURABILITY (2026-06-14): Render runs on a tier WITHOUT a persistent disk, so the
    25| * local *.json/*.jsonl files are wiped on every deploy/restart — the executive
    26| * brain would forget every learned goal/decision/preference between sessions. When
    27| * Supabase credentials are present, this store now persists to the SAME durable
    28| * Postgres document store the identity memory and business stores use, so the
    29| * brain truly remembers across logout, login, and redeploys. The filesystem path
    30| * remains the fallback for local dev / tests where Supabase is not configured.
    31| *
    32| * Runtime-light + deterministic: filesystem I/O or durable Supabase, no AI. Never
    33| * throws into callers — a failed persist is swallowed so remembering can never
    34| * break the action that produced the memory.
